# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Diagnostic dumps
_slsqp_diagnostic_*.npz

# Generated outputs (benchmark results, images). ``outputs`` may be a
# symlink to an external store,
# so match it with and without a trailing slash.
output/
outputs
outputs/

# User-specific MCP config (contains absolute paths)
.mcp.json

# JS tooling, should any be introduced
node_modules/

# Superseded internal notes kept beside the code they describe
# (docs/_archived, voigtfit/_archived). Matches at any depth.
_archived/

# Personal analysis / paper-figure scripts — kept out of the public
# repo pending case-by-case review of what is shareable.
/scripts/

# Internal-only documents (proposal drafts, business notes). Never
# pushed to the public repo.
_internal/

# Internal planning documents (factory/operations context). Never
# pushed to the public repo.
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

# Working notes, handoffs, audits and design records live under
# docs/_internal/ and are covered by the `_internal/` rule above. They
# are named there rather than here: listing each one individually put
# the filenames themselves in a public file, and did not catch new ones.
#
# Local working notes and handoffs. The GUI, web front end and depth
# pipeline that used to live here moved out on 2026-07-28 (see README);
# their ignore entries went with them.
#
# CLAUDE.md is unanchored on purpose: nested agent notes kept beside the
# code they describe (e.g. src/toyomacro/voigtfit/CLAUDE.md) stay local.
# Only the repository-root entry point is tracked.
CLAUDE.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# Local AI-agent working files. None of these ship in the sdist or
# wheel (see [tool.hatch.build.targets.sdist] and the CI archive
# assertion) — but the root AGENTS.md is tracked, as the shared,
# tool-agnostic instructions for this repository. Same unanchored
# pattern plus root exception as CLAUDE.md above.
.codex/
AGENTS.md
!/AGENTS.md

# Generated example data (regenerate: examples/data/make_example_data.py)
examples/data/*.h5
examples/output/
